<newsitem itemid="282656" id="root" date="1996-12-31" xml:lang="en">
<title>CHINA: China issues export tariff list for 1997.</title>
<headline>China issues export tariff list for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows export tariffs for 1997, provided by the State Council Customs Commission.</p>
<p>Figures represent percentages.</p>
<p>Temporary tariff rates apply from January 1 to December 31, 1997, to lead, zinc and tin ores and concentrates as well as unwrought zinc, in place of tariff rates which were officially listed, the commission said.</p>
<p>Where no temporary rate is given, the normal tariff rate applies.</p>
<p>Niobium tantalum and potassium tantaliflouride appeared on the list for the first time.</p>
<p>China imposes export tariffs on 35 items. Key minerals and ores are listed below:</p>
<p>	ITEMS		 TARIFF RATE     TEMPORARY RATE FOR 1997</p>
<p>Lead ores and</p>
<p>   concentrate		    30			5</p>
<p>Zinc ores and</p>
<p>   concentrate		    30			10</p>
<p>Tin ores and</p>
<p>   concentrate		    50			20</p>
<p>Tungsten ores and</p>
<p>   concentrate		    20</p>
<p>  Phosphorus			20</p>
<p>  Ferromanganese		  20</p>
<p>  Ferrosilicon		    25</p>
<p>  Unwrought zinc		  20			 0</p>
<p>  Unwrought nickel		40</p>
<p>  Unwrought aluminium	   30</p>
<p>  Unwrought antimony	    20</p>
<p>  Niobium tantalum		30</p>
<p>  Potassium tantaliflouride   30</p>
</text>
